Dear Dr Karl

I am working on 20 traits, is it possible to run scantwopermhk() on all the traits at the same time?

I tried using

operm2 <- scantwopermhk(SNP1, chr = 1:20, pheno.col = 2:21, n.perm = 1000, batchsize = 1000, verbose = TRUE, assumeCondIndep = TRUE)

But i get an error message that only one pheno.col is allowed. How can I run permutation on all the traits at the same time using scantwopermhk?

Kind regards
Celesta

